{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["Bars, etc., five — five rings on each plank on the outside, one below the other, to insert the bars into them, besides the middle bar that was inside the planks, which were all bored through to insert the middle bar inside, within the hollow of the planks. So there are the sockets below and the outer bars and the middle bar. Thus the strength of the middle bar inside them, within the hollow of the bore-holes of the planks, is great. According to the plain sense of Scripture: there were three middle bars, one on the north and one on the south and one on the west, from one end to the other. From the end of the northern wall to its other end, and likewise on the south and likewise on the west; and by means of the corner pieces the entire Tabernacle was joined together, all three of its walls at once — for the bars of the north and the south also entered into the corner pieces, since an amah of the corner piece covers the thickness of the plank of the second corner piece, and the ends of the bars of the north and south are fixed in the corner pieces. And according to the words of our Sages: the middle bar curved around inside the three walls, from end to end, by means of a miracle."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:43:13.413278466Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}